version: "0.3.0"
description: "A quieter Hermes Desktop with a crew view. Three themes (Helm Dark, Helm Graphite, Helm Paper) with matching terminal palettes; a Customize look page; status-bar chips for sessions working and the focused session's cost and context; and a Bots board that turns every profile into a rendered, customizable robot (10 toppers, 10 faces, 8 chest modules, 6 carried tools, 6 worn items, 7 colours, 191 PNG layers rendered in Blender) whose face is its live status: reply waiting, working, idle. Needs-you-first sorting and filters, each bot's latest session with Resume, New chat, recent spend, and a small robot left of the composer showing who you are talking to. Disclosure — desktop half uses only Desktop plugin SDK areas (themes, routes, sidebar nav, sidebarNav.prefs, palette, keybinds, statusBar.right, composer.leading, appearance.extra, a settings page); the themes' customCSS targets data-slot names (profile rail, pane tab, composer surface, tool block) the app ships, and JS never queries or edits app markup. Reads: host.profiles.list(), each bot's recent session rows via host.listPersistedSessions (title, timestamps, unread/active flags, cost; held in memory only), host.state busy/usage. Writes: its own ctx.storage (prefs, robot looks) and, only when changed on its settings page, the app's sessionListDensity and chatTextScale settings. Opens sessions, new chats, the profile folder (os.revealPath) and a gateway restart only on click. The dashboard half (dashboard/plugin_api.py) is a read-only FastAPI router at /api/plugins/helm/sprites that returns the bundled PNG layers as data URLs; names are matched against a fixed pattern, no path input reaches the filesystem, no writes. The agent half registers nothing. No network requests, no shell, no credentials, no telemetry. The Blender renderer used to make the PNGs is included under tools/render/ (not run by Hermes)."
